.TH HTTPJET 1 "October 2026" "httpjet" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
httpjet \- HTTP server with LiteSpeed-compatible XML configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B httpjet
.RI [ --root " directory" ]
.RI [ command " [options]" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
httpjet is a Linux web server using io_uring. The packaged service serves
static files over HTTP on port 80 as the dedicated httpjet system account.
TLS, PHP, page caching, metrics and management listeners are disabled in the
default service configuration.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check --strict
Validate configuration without serving requests. This is also the default
command when no command is supplied.
.TP
.B serve
Run the server using the supplied configuration and listener options.
.TP
.B doctor
Report installation and runtime prerequisites without changing system settings.
.TP
.B --help
Show the complete command and option reference. Individual commands also
accept this option.
.TP
.B --version
Show the server version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/httpjet/conf/httpd_config.xml
Default server configuration.
.TP
.B /etc/httpjet/conf/vhosts/default.xml
Default virtual host configuration and static-only PHP suffix denial.
.TP
.B /var/www/httpjet
Website document root. Existing content is preserved across package operations.
.TP
.B /usr/share/httpjet/welcome/index.html
Canonical welcome template, copied only when the package creates a new document root.
.TP
.B /var/log/httpjet
Packaged service access and error logs. Service diagnostics are also in the journal.
.SH SERVICE MANAGEMENT
Use systemctl start, stop, restart or status with httpjet.service. An upgrade
restarts a running service after strict configuration validation; a stopped
service remains stopped. Configuration changes take effect on service restart.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.PP
https://httpjet.net/docs/
